, feeling intimidated in music theory discussions (s23-s24), and friction with a band over artistic direction leading to leaving the band (s4-s5). The original question's description of stifling band disagreements is consistent with s4-s5. The summary synthesizes these compatible facts into one whole account.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"autonomy_pref\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_928a9cee2f955304a6a858d9\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user currently prefers and desires creative autonomy, seeking to work independently on personal music projects that allow for authentic self-expression, emotional connection, and personal growth, having been discouraged by past collaborative conflicts and feeling more fulfilled when creating alone.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s60\", \"s61\", \"s4\", \"s42\", \"s5\", \"s43\", \"s39\", \"s41\", \"s40\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"current\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user describes challenges with collaboration due to differing artistic visions (s4, s5), expresses that technical production did not resonate and that true passion lies in emotional connection and creating personal tracks (s39, s40, s41, s42, s43), and contrasts passive consumption (documentary) with the deeper engagement of personal creation (s60, s61). These statements collectively support a current preference for autonomous, independent creative work.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"response\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_a6c71e91466ce04d07052e6b\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"I understand that initially, you enjoyed collaborating with other musicians, finding it an enriching creative experience. However, o